{"step_index":7717,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T16:28:24Z","thinking":"The absence of a background task allows for controlled modification of several code files before server launch, preventing potential conflicts.  The first verification targets modifications within a specific application file, focusing on a function related to chat resetting.\n\n\nAttempting a faster chat reset by sending an escape keypress before locating the \"new chat\" button. This initial step might circumvent potential delays. If the UI reset fails after the escape, it will proceed to a full page reload, including a short timeout to prevent the Playwright agent from stalling.\n\n\nA quick UI check after the escape keypress assesses if a text area element indicates a successful chat reset, logging accordingly.  If this UI-based reset fails, the process falls back to navigating to a new chat session to ensure a fresh start. Subsequently, ensures the target model is selected and the system is in the proper state.\n\n\nExamining the DOM to identify model turns within the chat history, focusing on filtering out user turns. Initial logic was revised in one file, now checking several attributes and element characteristics to accurately distinguish model turns, including author labels and CSS classes. The secondary file was then checked to ensure alignment in approach. Discrepancies between the original and revised filters are highlighted, to decide which definition to use.\n\n\nInitial logic for turn detection in the chat history is flawed; the current implementation incorrectly identifies user turns as model turns. The presence of a specific element is incorrectly used to determine the turn type. The definition of \"new turn\" also causes a false positive, incorrectly identifying turns. Now evaluating potential fixes for robust turn detection.\n\n\nRevised the turn detection logic, focusing on identifying model turns within the chat history more accurately.  Several factors are considered: role attributes, CSS classes, author labels, and the presence of specific content types. The initial approach filtered incorrectly. It's now filtering out user turns. Now, counting the model turns after filtering and checking if a new turn started. This revised detection is a major step.\n\n\nA state transition from \"no response\" to \"response in progress\" occurs based on three factors.  These factors are the visibility of a model activity indicator, the start of a new model turn, or the presence of text being emitted by the model.  This logic ensures that the system accurately tracks when the model starts generating a response. If these conditions are not met within a predefined timeout, an error is logged, indicating a failure to start generation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"D:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio\\\\app.py\"","EndLine":"490","StartLine":"425","toolAction":"\"View start of send_prompt_and_stream\"","toolSummary":"\"View send_prompt_and_stream lines 425-490\""}}]}
